## Verifying the download

`SHA256SUMS` sits next to the tarball (it is not inside this archive) and
covers every `.tar.gz` and `.spdx.json` artifact:

```sh
sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS
```

When the release was signed, `SHA256SUMS.asc` and `KEYS.asc` are published as
well:

```sh
gpg --import KEYS.asc
gpg --verify SHA256SUMS.asc SHA256SUMS
```

If those two files are absent the release is **unsigned**: `SHA256SUMS` still
detects corruption and tampering in transit, but it provides no provenance.
